NEARS-1110 QA — PRE-EXISTING (regression_bug, NOT caused by this change)
Surface: any bottom sheet (observed on the item-detail sheet) with app locale = Arabic.

With the app switched to Arabic, every NEARS-1110 string renders correctly in
Arabic, but the modal bottom-sheet's barrier/scrim accessibility label is still
the English framework default 'Dismiss'. It is a Flutter MaterialLocalizations
label, not a GetX `.tr` key, so it is unaffected by (and out of scope for)
this ticket -- it points at a missing/partial Arabic MaterialLocalizations
delegate in the app's GetMaterialApp config.

Observed (raw uiautomator content-desc dump, locale = ar, item sheet open):
  [content-desc] 'خطأ في الخادم'
  [content-desc] 'نحن نواجه مشاكل حاليًا. يرجى المحاولة بعد قليل.'
  [content-desc] 'أعد المحاولة'
  [content-desc] 'Dismiss'          <-- untranslated framework barrier label

Severity: low (a11y/i18n polish; screen-reader only, no visible text).
Not blocking NEARS-1110.
